    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d644">

                <pb facs="0617" n="605" xml:id="pg605"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">741.61/890: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-05-29T23:00:00+03:00">May 29, 1940—11
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 29—8:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>600. Embassy’s telegram No. 584, May 25.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d644-f1"/> A Tass
                    despatch was issued tonight stating that Molotov has instructed Maiski to advise
                    the British Government that the proposed mission to Moscow of Sir Stafford
                    Cripps is unacceptable to the Soviet Government and that if the British
                    Government desires to conduct trade negotiations with the Soviet Government “and
                    not simply confine itself to talk of a nonexistent change in the relations
                    between England and the Soviet Union” it can do so through its Ambassador at
                    Moscow, Mr. William Seeds,<anchor n="5" xml:id="d644-f2"/> or in the event that
                    he is not returning to his post, through his successor.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d644-f1" n="4" xml:id="d644-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d644-f2" n="5" xml:id="d644-f2-content">
                <p>Sir William Seeds, British Ambassador to the Soviet Union since January 1939, who
                    left after the outbreak of the Finnish-Soviet war.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
